## Plan — Section 2 (final revision): Expose launch argv as a common system-prompt section

**Problem:** The LLM can't self-identify as a skill-manager peer because `--role` (and all other launch flags) are invisible to it. The role is only used for `PeerManager` identity registration, never injected into the prompt.

**Design:** Add a `getLaunchArgs()` export in `config.ts` that returns a sanitized summary of the CLI flags (secrets filtered), then add a `buildLaunchArgsSection()` in `agent-prompts.ts` that injects it into `buildCommonSections()` — so it appears in **every** prompt variant (solo, team, plan, teammate).

### Part A — `config.ts`: export sanitized launch args

Add a new function:

```typescript
/** Secret-bearing flags that must NEVER appear in the system prompt. */
const SECRET_FLAGS = ['ollama-api-key', 'deepseek-api-key'];

/**
 * Return a sanitized summary of the CLI flags this instance was launched with,
 * suitable for inclusion in the system prompt. Secret-bearing flags
 * (--ollama-api-key, --deepseek-api-key) are redacted to `--<flag> ***`.
 */
export function getLaunchArgs(): string {
  const parts: string[] = [];
  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(args)) {
    if (key === '_') continue;              // positional args
    if (SECRET_FLAGS.includes(key)) {
      parts.push(`--${key} ***`);
      continue;
    }
    if (value === true) {
      parts.push(`--${key}`);
    } else if (value === false || value === null || value === undefined) {
      continue;                             // flag not set
    } else {
      parts.push(`--${key} ${value}`);
    }
  }
  return parts.length > 0 ? parts.join(' ') : '(none)';
}
```

This reads from the already-parsed module-private `args` object, so no re-parsing. Secrets are redacted to `***`, not dropped — the LLM sees that a key was provided without learning its value.

### Part B — `agent-prompts.ts`: add launch-args section to common sections

Add a new helper:

```typescript
import { getLaunchArgs } from '../config.js';

function buildLaunchArgsSection(): string {
  return `## Launch Args\nYou were started with: \`${getLaunchArgs()}\``;
}
```

Add it to `buildCommonSections()`:

```typescript
function buildCommonSections(): string {
  return [
    buildLaunchArgsSection(),    // NEW
    '',
    buildVerificationSection(),
    '',
    buildPlatformSection(),
    // ... rest unchanged
  ].join('\n');
}
```

Since `buildCommonSections()` is called by `buildSoloNormalPrompt`, `buildTeamNormalPrompt`, and `buildTeammatePrompt`, the launch args appear in all normal-mode prompts. For plan mode, add it to `buildPlanBasePrompt` as well (plan mode doesn't use `buildCommonSections()` — it assembles its own sections).

**What the skill-manager peer sees in its system prompt:**

```
## Launch Args
You were started with: `--auto --role skill-manager --skip-healthcheck`
```

**What a normal lead sees:**

```
## Launch Args
You were started with: `(none)`
```

No special-casing, no `if (role)` branching — the LLM reads its argv and self-identifies.

